  "description": "The person's per-child switch of the owner-approved question route (zerus-sa9qn.32 and .33): whether a supervised Claude child's blocking questions go to its parent session. Kept on the child's computer (`hgs question-routing`, marker session-question-routing-v1) and shared by every desktop and phone. The desktop (client/core and client/src), the connector, Android and iOS follow this contract. parse: the row's or inspection's `question_routing` value (null when unknown, never a default); under marker session-question-routing-v2 it also carries person_off, a display-only mirror of the person's latch in the computer's desktop service (zerus-sa9qn.50), whose Store latch is the authority. availability: whether a session's actions show the switch and whether it can be changed while its computer is online and supports the operation. change: the exact payload that turns the current value the other way at its revision. results: how each platform settles the computer's reply: confirmed, refused (a closed refusal) or uncertain (never retried).",
